From 4b7e9df766419b5db83e9543702b8802b801a103 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RivonClaw CI <ci@rivonclaw.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 17:44:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] vendor(openclaw): backport Feishu visible delivery custody
 fix

Why:
- The pinned vendor includes durable ambiguous-delivery notices but predates upstream commit 1096ca2a708, so visible Feishu CardKit replies can remain unknown and emit a false warning on the next inbound turn.
- Feishu notice debt created before the custody fix survives upgrades; clear it silently instead of injecting transport prose into a real conversation.

Removal:
- Drop the custody backport when .openclaw-version includes upstream commit 1096ca2a708f600386b6efd349823c759e041fcc (fix(feishu): retain partial custody on preview cleanup).
- Drop the Feishu notice suppression after all supported Desktop versions include that upstream fix and pre-backport notice debt has aged out, or when upstream provides channel-appropriate silent reconciliation.

Tests:
- apps/desktop/src/channels/vendor-feishu-visible-delivery-custody.sentinel.test.ts
- vendor/openclaw/src/channels/turn/pending-delivery-notice.test.ts
- vendor/openclaw/src/channels/turn/run-channel-turn.custody.test.ts
- vendor/openclaw/extensions/feishu/src/delivery-trace.test.ts
